You'll notice that two deities are missing from the above tables. Each
of these deities would have very special behaviour indeed.
* The Lady will never respond to prayer, sacrifice or blasphemy, but
will apportion gifts and punishments at mostly random intervals. She
is, however, more likely to dispatch spectacular rewards when one is
on the brink of certain death, and more likely to unleash spectacular
disasters when one has a low Luck stat. See also the "Xom" god in
Linley's Dungeon Crawl.
* As for Crom... "It was useless to call on Crom, because he was a
gloomy, savage god, and he hated weaklings. But he gave a man courage
at birth, and the will and might to kill his enemies, which, in the
Cimmerian's mind, was all any god should be expected to do." -- The
Tower of the Elephant, by Robert E. Howard.

